<html>
<body>
Reports the comma form of the
<a href="https://sass-lang.com/documentation/breaking-changes/if-function/">Sass <code>if()</code> function</a>.
Dart Sass 1.95.0 deprecated it, and plans to remove it in Dart Sass 3.0.0.
Use the CSS-style form instead.
<p><b>Example:</b></p>
<pre><code>
.a {
  width: if($wide, 70%, 50%);
}
</code></pre>
<p>After the quick fix:</p>
<pre><code>
.a {
  width: if(sass($wide): 70%; else: 50%);
}
</code></pre>
<!-- tooltip end -->
</body>
</html>
